+Method and source bounds:
+
+- Read pinned GitHub blobs and complete recursive trees through `gh`, including all 16 book chapters, the three accompanying architecture/terminology documents, eight module README/spec documents, the session-host gate guide, ten requested CIPs, and the launcher README/SPEC: **40 primary prose documents**. Decision 0021 and the book build script are supporting sources. The source register below identifies each revision; PR heads are proposals at those revisions, not merged-main assertions.
+- A groups clauses only when they share a source and disposition. Narrative motivations, operational claims, examples and expressly open questions are included separately from normative requirements. Every chapter, including the postscript, has entries. A coverage status reports documentary coverage, never implementation coverage.
+- **COVERED** means a cited specification or decision defines the clause. **ARCH-ONLY** means the platform architecture defines it but the audited module/CIP contracts do not: this is **MISSING module-level coverage**. **CONFLICTING** identifies incompatible instructions or an unqualified claim contradicted elsewhere. **MISSING** means no defining contract in the audited corpus, not absence from every repository. **OPEN** preserves an explicitly unresolved choice. **UNVERIFIED** marks empirical assertions not established by this read-only audit.
+- Diagram inspection covers the recursively listed `.puml`, `.dsl`, and image files in the requested repositories/paths, plus textual state/layout sketches. The book has 26 PNGs and seven same-stem source files; the other inventories are in B. Embedded PlantUML metadata was read for every PNG; the container map and worker-start render were also visually inspected. No product, test suite, diagram renderer, or deployment was executed.
+- Absence claims are bounded to the pinned complete trees and named paths. A binary image has no repository line numbers: its inventory entry links the image, and cites its embedding prose or the architecture's diagram-source declaration. Text/source citations include line ranges and the nearest section in the link title. Unavailable external specifications are not silently treated as absent.
+- Source material stays at its original repository links. This report contains findings and locators, not copied research corpora. No LOGBOOK was changed; the task's explicit prohibition takes precedence over the generic logbook checklist.
